[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5429307365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122848#issuecomment-5429307365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122848","id":5429307365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ5yn5Q","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T18:16:18Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T18:16:18Z","body":"> Should we clamp the mouse X/Y coordinates to the visible coordinates? Currently, if your mouse cursor goes outside the viewport (e.g. on the inspector), it will still update the mouse coordinates in the View Information panel.\r\n\r\nWhat is the purpose of displaying the mouse X/Y coordinates in the first place?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5429307365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5429359364","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122848#issuecomment-5429359364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122848","id":5429359364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ51zBA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T18:21:05Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T18:41:10Z","body":"> What is the purpose of displaying the mouse X/Y coordinates in the first place?\t\r\n\r\nThere was an old issue on the subject with some use cases described: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/6224\r\n\r\nThis was mostly done for consistency with the 3D panel which shows the camera coordinates, where it's useful to troubleshoot precision issues. Floating-point precision issues are much less common in 2D games, so it's less important to have here.\r\n\r\n**Edit:** Removed mouse coordinates display.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5429359364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"mi